      \field{labeltitlesource}{shorttitle}
      \field{abstract}{We present a novel dataset captured from a VW station wagon for use in mobile robotics and autonomous driving research. In total, we recorded 6 hours of trafﬁc scenarios at 10-100 Hz using a variety of sensor modalities such as highresolution color and grayscale stereo cameras, a Velodyne 3D laser scanner and a high-precision GPS/IMU inertial navigation system. The scenarios are diverse, capturing real-world trafﬁc situations and range from freeways over rural areas to innercity scenes with many static and dynamic objects. Our data is calibrated, synchronized and timestamped, and we provide the rectiﬁed and raw image sequences. Our dataset also contains object labels in the form of 3D tracklets and we provide online benchmarks for stereo, optical ﬂow, object detection and other tasks. This paper describes our recording platform, the data format and the utilities that we provide.}
